<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/UseProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The UseProcess is an abstract class used to define processes that interact with key elements. Plan, state, and inspection processes plus managing boundaries are critical processes used by elements.\n\nRelationship:\n\nFor each UseProcess or subclass except the PlanProcess there is at least one /Core/Relationship class or subclass with the relationshipType of 'affects’ on the from and a /Core/Element class or subclass on the to."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/contains> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The from Element contains each to Element."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship describes if a vulnerability is\nlisted in any exploit catalog such as the\nCISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog <https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog>.\n\n*Constraints*\n\n- The relationship type shall be set to hasAssessmentFor.\n\n*Example*\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"security_ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship\",\n  \"spdxId\": \"urn:spdx.dev:exploit-catalog-1\",\n  \"relationshipType\": \"hasAssessmentFor\",\n  \"security_catalogType\": \"kev\",\n  \"locator\": \"https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\",\n  \"security_exploited\": \"true\",\n  \"from\": \"urn:spdx.dev:vuln-cve-2023-2136\",\n  \"to\": [\"urn:product-google-chrome-112.0.5615.136\"],\n  \"suppliedBy\": \"urn:spdx.dev:agent-jane-doe\",\n  \"security_publishedTime\": \"2021-03-09T11:04:53Z\"\n}"@en .
